<section id="A0.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A0.SS1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text">-A</span> </span><span id="A0.SS1.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 ‣ IV Main Results ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span>
</h3>

<section id="A0.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="A0.SS1.SSS1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text">-A</span>1 </span>Statement <a href="#S4.I1.i1" title="item 1 ‣ Theorem 1 ‣ IV Main Results ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>
</h4>

<div id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">By the hypotheses of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 ‣ IV Main Results ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{F}_{h})\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{F}_{h})\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the hard-constrained QP (<a href="#S3.E22" title="In III-D Enforcing Constraints via Soft-Constrained Optimisation ‣ III Methodology ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) (with <math id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>) is feasible. By the theory of exact penalty functions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="Soft constraints and exact penalty functions in model predictive control" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>, for a sufficiently large penalty weight <math id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> exceeding the optimal Lagrange multiplier of the hard-constrained QP, the soft-constrained QP solution satisfies <math id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}^{*}=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}^{*}=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the control torque (<a href="#S3.E24" title="In III-D Enforcing Constraints via Soft-Constrained Optimisation ‣ III Methodology ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) satisfies <math id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}\in\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}\in\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> by construction.
 ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="A0.SS1.SSS2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text">-A</span>2 </span>Statement <a href="#S4.I1.i2" title="item 2 ‣ Theorem 1 ‣ IV Main Results ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>
</h4>

<div id="A0.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The CBF constraints (<a href="#S3.E22.2" title="In 22 ‣ III-D Enforcing Constraints via Soft-Constrained Optimisation ‣ III Methodology ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22b</span></a>) are hard in (<a href="#S3.E22" title="In III-D Enforcing Constraints via Soft-Constrained Optimisation ‣ III Methodology ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) and are never relaxed by <math id="A0.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. The result follows from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="Nonsmooth Barrier Functions With Applications to Multi-Robot Systems" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, Thm. 1]</cite>, Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4 ([28]) ‣ IV Main Results ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, and (<a href="#S3.E22.2" title="In 22 ‣ III-D Enforcing Constraints via Soft-Constrained Optimisation ‣ III Methodology ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22b</span></a>).
 ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="A0.SS1.SSS3.5.1.1" class="ltx_text">-A</span>3 </span>Statement <a href="#S4.I1.i3" title="item 3 ‣ Theorem 1 ‣ IV Main Results ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>
</h4>

<div id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The proof employs a composite Lyapunov approach. We first analyse the reference-model subsystem (<math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>) using <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the impedance tracking subsystem using <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>mm</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p2.10" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}\coloneqq\boldsymbol{\theta}-\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}\coloneqq\boldsymbol{\theta}-\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}\coloneqq\mathbf{w}-\hat{\mathbf{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}\coloneqq\mathbf{w}-\hat{\mathbf{w}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall that <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p2.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}=\mathbf{q}_{\mathrm{ref}}-\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐪</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}=\mathbf{q}_{\mathrm{ref}}-\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, which has dynamics <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p2.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddot{\mathbf{e}}=\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{ref}}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{\mathbf{e}}=\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{ref}}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>. From (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In III-B Safety-Filtered Reference Model and NCBF Design ‣ III Methodology ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p2.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{ref}}=\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{cmd}}+\mathbf{K}_{v}(\dot{\mathbf{q}}-\dot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{ref}})+\mathbf{K}_{p}(\mathbf{q}-\mathbf{q}_{\mathrm{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>cmd</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{ref}}=\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{cmd}}+\mathbf{K}_{v}(\dot{\mathbf{q}}-\dot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{ref}})+\mathbf{K}_{p}(\mathbf{q}-\mathbf{q}_{\mathrm{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting (<a href="#S3.E17" title="In III-C Fuzzy Logic and Disturbance Observer Design ‣ III Methodology ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) into (<a href="#S3.E18" title="In III-C Fuzzy Logic and Disturbance Observer Design ‣ III Methodology ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) gives <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p2.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{d}_{\mathrm{CBF}}(t)=-\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}-\mathbf{e}_{d}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐝</mi><mi>CBF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝜻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{d}_{\mathrm{CBF}}(t)=-\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}-\mathbf{e}_{d}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, thus (<a href="#S3.E15" title="In III-C Fuzzy Logic and Disturbance Observer Design ‣ III Methodology ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) can be rewritten as <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p2.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddot{\mathbf{q}}=\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{cmd}}+\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{s}}-\mathbf{e}_{d}-\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>cmd</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝜻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{\mathbf{q}}=\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{cmd}}+\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{s}}-\mathbf{e}_{d}-\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p2.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddot{\mathbf{e}}=-\mathbf{K}_{v}\dot{\mathbf{e}}-\mathbf{K}_{p}\mathbf{e}+\mathbf{e}_{d}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{s}}+\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝜻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{\mathbf{e}}=-\mathbf{K}_{v}\dot{\mathbf{e}}-\mathbf{K}_{p}\mathbf{e}+\mathbf{e}_{d}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{s}}+\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. As such, <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p2.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\mathbf{r}}=-\mathbf{K}_{r}\mathbf{r}+\mathbf{e}_{d}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{s}}+\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝜻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\mathbf{r}}=-\mathbf{K}_{r}\mathbf{r}+\mathbf{e}_{d}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{s}}+\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> (follows from the definitions of <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p2.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}_{v},\mathbf{K}_{p},\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}_{v},\mathbf{K}_{p},\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p3.11" class="ltx_p">Consider the Lyapunov function candidate</p>
<table id="A0.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{1}=\tfrac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{r}\|^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Gamma}_{\theta}^{-1}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}+\tfrac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Gamma}_{w}^{-1}\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{1}=\tfrac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{r}\|^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Gamma}_{\theta}^{-1}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}+\tfrac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Gamma}_{w}^{-1}\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which is positive-definite and radially unbounded (Rayleigh-Ritz Theorem). Differentiating and substituting (<a href="#S4.E28" title="In Theorem 1 ‣ IV Main Results ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E29" title="In Theorem 1 ‣ IV Main Results ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) with <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\boldsymbol{\phi}}_{\theta}=\dot{\boldsymbol{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\boldsymbol{\phi}}_{\theta}=\dot{\boldsymbol{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p3.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\boldsymbol{\psi}}_{w}=-\dot{\hat{\mathbf{w}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝍</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\boldsymbol{\psi}}_{w}=-\dot{\hat{\mathbf{w}}}</annotation></semantics></math> gives:</p>
<table id="A0.E37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A0.E37X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.E37X.2.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{V}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{V}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.E37X.3.2.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{r}^{\top}(-\mathbf{K}_{r}\mathbf{r}+\mathbf{e}_{d}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{s}+\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝜻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{r}^{\top}(-\mathbf{K}_{r}\mathbf{r}+\mathbf{e}_{d}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{s}+\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td>
</tr>
<tr id="A0.E37Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.E37Xa.2.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}^{\top}\operatorname{Proj}_{\boldsymbol{\Gamma}_{\theta}}\!\big(\boldsymbol{\theta},-\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})\mathbf{r},f(\boldsymbol{\theta}))+\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}|\mathbf{r}|-\sigma_{w}\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}\hat{\mathbf{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi>𝚪</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝜻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}^{\top}\operatorname{Proj}_{\boldsymbol{\Gamma}_{\theta}}\!\big(\boldsymbol{\theta},-\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})\mathbf{r},f(\boldsymbol{\theta}))+\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}|\mathbf{r}|-\sigma_{w}\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}\hat{\mathbf{w}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr>
<tr id="A0.E37Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.E37Xb.2.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbf{r}^{\top}(-\mathbf{K}_{r}\mathbf{r}+\mathbf{e}_{d}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{s}+\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝜻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbf{r}^{\top}(-\mathbf{K}_{r}\mathbf{r}+\mathbf{e}_{d}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{s}+\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr>
<tr id="A0.E37Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.E37Xc.2.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})\mathbf{r}+\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}|\mathbf{r}|-\sigma_{w}\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}\hat{\mathbf{w}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\zeta}(\boldsymbol{\xi})\mathbf{r}+\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}|\mathbf{r}|-\sigma_{w}\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}\hat{\mathbf{w}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p3.10" class="ltx_p">The cross terms <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p3.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\zeta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\zeta}\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜻</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\zeta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\zeta}\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math> cancel, and using <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p3.4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}^{\top}\mathbf{e}_{d}\leq|\mathbf{r}|^{\top}\mathbf{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}^{\top}\mathbf{e}_{d}\leq|\mathbf{r}|^{\top}\mathbf{w}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p3.5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathbf{r}|^{\top}\mathbf{w}-\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}|\mathbf{r}|=|\mathbf{r}|^{\top}\hat{\mathbf{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathbf{r}|^{\top}\mathbf{w}-\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}|\mathbf{r}|=|\mathbf{r}|^{\top}\hat{\mathbf{w}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 ([21]) ‣ IV Main Results ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> gives <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p3.6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq|\mathbf{r}|^{\top}\hat{\mathbf{w}}-\mathbf{r}^{\top}\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{s}\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq|\mathbf{r}|^{\top}\hat{\mathbf{w}}-\mathbf{r}^{\top}\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{s}\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p3.7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\sum_{i}\varepsilon_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\sum_{i}\varepsilon_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying the Cauchy-Schwartz and Young’s Inequalities to the leakage term yields <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p3.8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{w}\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}\hat{\mathbf{w}}\leq-\frac{1}{2}\sigma_{w}\|\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}\|^{2}+\frac{1}{2}\sigma_{w}W^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{w}\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}\hat{\mathbf{w}}\leq-\frac{1}{2}\sigma_{w}\|\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}\|^{2}+\frac{1}{2}\sigma_{w}W^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we have <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p3.9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{V}_{1}\leq-\mathbf{r}^{\top}\mathbf{K}_{r}\mathbf{r}-\tfrac{1}{2}\sigma_{w}\|\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}\|^{2}+\epsilon+K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{V}_{1}\leq-\mathbf{r}^{\top}\mathbf{K}_{r}\mathbf{r}-\tfrac{1}{2}\sigma_{w}\|\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}\|^{2}+\epsilon+K</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p3.10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\tfrac{1}{2}\sigma_{w}W^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\tfrac{1}{2}\sigma_{w}W^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p4.7" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p4.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}=(\mathbf{r},\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta},\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w})\in\mathbb{R}^{2n+N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}=(\mathbf{r},\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta},\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w})\in\mathbb{R}^{2n+N}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p4.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}=\min{\left(2\lambda_{\min}(\mathbf{K}_{r}),\,\sigma_{w}\lambda_{\min}(\boldsymbol{\Gamma}_{w})\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚪</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}=\min{\left(2\lambda_{\min}(\mathbf{K}_{r}),\,\sigma_{w}\lambda_{\min}(\boldsymbol{\Gamma}_{w})\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p4.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\theta}=\tfrac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Gamma}_{\theta}^{-1}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\theta}=\tfrac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Gamma}_{\theta}^{-1}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the projection operator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="Projection Operator in Adaptive Systems" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite> and Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 ‣ III-C Fuzzy Logic and Disturbance Observer Design ‣ III Methodology ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p4.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}\right\|\leq\Phi_{\max}\implies V_{\theta}\leq V_{\theta,\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\boldsymbol{\phi}_{\theta}\right\|\leq\Phi_{\max}\implies V_{\theta}\leq V_{\theta,\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, thus it follows that <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p4.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-(\tfrac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{r}\|^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Gamma}_{w}^{-1}\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w})=-V_{1}+V_{\theta}\leq-V_{1}+V_{\theta,\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-(\tfrac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{r}\|^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Gamma}_{w}^{-1}\boldsymbol{\psi}_{w})=-V_{1}+V_{\theta}\leq-V_{1}+V_{\theta,\max}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting this into <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p4.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{V}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{V}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p4.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{V}_{1}\leq-z_{1}V_{1}+(\epsilon+K+z_{1}V_{\theta,\max})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{V}_{1}\leq-z_{1}V_{1}+(\epsilon+K+z_{1}V_{\theta,\max})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p5.5" class="ltx_p">By the comparison lemma <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="Nonlinear Systems" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p5.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p5.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, is UUB. Since <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p5.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive-definite and <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p5.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\mathbf{e}}=-\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{e}+\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\mathbf{e}}=-\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{e}+\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is a stable first-order linear time-invariant (LTI) system, the vector <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p5.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{e},\dot{\mathbf{e}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{e},\dot{\mathbf{e}})</annotation></semantics></math> is UUB.</p>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p6.12" class="ltx_p">Define the impedance filtered error</p>
<table id="A0.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{imp}}=\dot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{imp}}+\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{imp}},\quad\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{imp}}=\mathbf{q}_{\mathrm{imp}}-\mathbf{q}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>imp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>imp</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>imp</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>imp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>imp</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐪</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{imp}}=\dot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{imp}}+\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{imp}},\quad\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{imp}}=\mathbf{q}_{\mathrm{imp}}-\mathbf{q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p6.11" class="ltx_p">Now, we consider the <em id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p6.11.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">model impedance mismatch</em>. Let <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p6.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{mm}}=\mathbf{q}_{\mathrm{imp}}-\mathbf{q}_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>mm</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>imp</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{mm}}=\mathbf{q}_{\mathrm{imp}}-\mathbf{q}_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p6.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}=\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{imp}}-\mathbf{r}=\dot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{mm}}+\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{mm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>mm</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>imp</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>mm</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>mm</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}=\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{imp}}-\mathbf{r}=\dot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{mm}}+\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{mm}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The mismatch error has dynamics <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p6.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{mm}}=\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{imp}}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>mm</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>imp</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{mm}}=\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{imp}}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall from Section <a href="#S3.SS4" title="III-D Enforcing Constraints via Soft-Constrained Optimisation ‣ III Methodology ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag"><span class="ltx_text">III-D</span></span></a> that <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p6.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}=\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{nom}}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{cmd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>QP</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>nom</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>cmd</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}=\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{nom}}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{cmd}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p6.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{nom}}=\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{cmd}}+\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>nom</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>cmd</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>QP</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{nom}}=\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{cmd}}+\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p6.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{cmd}}=(\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{imp}}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}})+\mathbf{K}_{v}\dot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{mm}}+\mathbf{K}_{p}\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{mm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>cmd</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>imp</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>QP</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>mm</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>mm</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{cmd}}=(\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{imp}}-\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}})+\mathbf{K}_{v}\dot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{mm}}+\mathbf{K}_{p}\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{mm}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p6.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{mm}}=-\mathbf{K}_{v}\dot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{mm}}-\mathbf{K}_{p}\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{mm}}+\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>mm</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>mm</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>mm</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>QP</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{mm}}=-\mathbf{K}_{v}\dot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{mm}}-\mathbf{K}_{p}\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{mm}}+\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p6.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\mathbf{r}}_{\mathrm{mm}}=-\mathbf{K}_{r}\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}+\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>mm</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>mm</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>QP</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\mathbf{r}}_{\mathrm{mm}}=-\mathbf{K}_{r}\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}+\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p6.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{cmd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>cmd</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{cmd}}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by the hard acceleration box constraints in (<a href="#S3.E22" title="In III-D Enforcing Constraints via Soft-Constrained Optimisation ‣ III Methodology ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>), and <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p6.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{nom}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>nom</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{nom}}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by construction; hence <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p6.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>QP</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded.</p>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7.14" class="ltx_p">Consider the Lyapunov function candidate</p>
<table id="A0.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{2}=\tfrac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}\|^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>mm</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{2}=\tfrac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7.13" class="ltx_p">which is positive-definite and radially unbounded (Rayleigh-Ritz Theorem). Differentiating <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{V_{2}}=-\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}^{\top}\mathbf{K}_{r}\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}+\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}^{\top}\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>mm</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>mm</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>mm</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>QP</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{V_{2}}=-\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}^{\top}\mathbf{K}_{r}\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}+\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}^{\top}\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Cauchy-Schwartz, we have <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{V_{2}}\leq-\lambda_{\min}(\mathbf{K}_{r})\left\|\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}\right\|^{2}+\left\|\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}\right\|\left\|\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>mm</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>mm</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>QP</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{V_{2}}\leq-\lambda_{\min}(\mathbf{K}_{r})\left\|\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}\right\|^{2}+\left\|\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}\right\|\left\|\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}\right\|</annotation></semantics></math> and applying Young’s Inequality gives <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{V_{2}}\leq-\lambda_{\min}(\mathbf{K}_{r})V_{2}+\tfrac{1}{2\lambda_{\min}(\mathbf{K}_{r})}\left\|\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>QP</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{V_{2}}\leq-\lambda_{\min}(\mathbf{K}_{r})V_{2}+\tfrac{1}{2\lambda_{\min}(\mathbf{K}_{r})}\left\|\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the comparison lemma <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="Nonlinear Systems" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>mm</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}</annotation></semantics></math> is UUB. From (<a href="#A0.E38" title="In -A3 Statement 3 ‣ -A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>), <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{imp}}=\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}+\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>imp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>mm</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{imp}}=\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}+\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, thus <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{imp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>imp</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{imp}}</annotation></semantics></math> is UUB. <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{imp}}=-\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{imp}}+\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{imp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>imp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>imp</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>imp</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{imp}}=-\boldsymbol{\Lambda}\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{imp}}+\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{imp}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a stable first-order LTI system; thus, the vector <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{imp}},\dot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{imp}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>imp</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>imp</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{imp}},\dot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{imp}})</annotation></semantics></math> is UUB. In the special case where <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}\right\|=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mi>QP</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\ddot{\mathbf{q}}_{\mathrm{QP}}\right\|=0</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., no QP constraints are active), <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>mm</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{mm}}</annotation></semantics></math> is asymptotically stable; thus, <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{imp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>imp</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{\mathrm{imp}}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p7.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p8.6" class="ltx_p">Finally, as <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p8.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{imp}},\dot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{imp}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>imp</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>imp</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{e}_{\mathrm{imp}},\dot{\mathbf{e}}_{\mathrm{imp}})</annotation></semantics></math> is UUB, then with Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 ‣ IV Main Results ‣ Safety-Critical Adaptive Impedance Control via Nonsmooth Control Barrier Functions under State and Input Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, there exists <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p8.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p8.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mathbf{z}_{\mathrm{imp}}(t)-\mathbf{z}(t)\right\|\leq\rho(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>imp</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mathbf{z}_{\mathrm{imp}}(t)-\mathbf{z}(t)\right\|\leq\rho(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p8.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p8.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is some class-<math id="A0.SS1.SSS3.p8.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> function.
 ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
